<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%- include('include/head', { title: 'Coloring — ASIM 3310', extraCSS: ['generative.css'] }) %>
  <style>
    .gradient-asim { background: linear-gradient(160deg, #d0ecd8 0%, #e8f0d0 50%, #f8f0c8 100%) !important; }
    nav { --nav-bg: rgba(208,236,216,0.95); background: rgba(208,236,216,0.85); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(120,180,130,0.2); }

    .work-content { max-width: 1400px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 var(--side); }

    .video-full { max-width: 1400px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 var(--side) 1rem; }
    .video-full-wrap {
      width: 100%; border-radius: 16px; overflow: hidden;
      background: #0e0a1a; aspect-ratio: 16/9;
    }
    .video-full-wrap video {
      width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover;
      display: block; border-radius: 16px;
    }
    .video-caption {
      margin-top: 0.6rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;
      font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.15rem;
      font-style: italic; color: var(--text-light);
    }

    /* Full width image */
    .img-full { max-width: 1400px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 var(--side) 2rem; }
    .img-full img {
      width: 100%; border-radius: 16px;
      display: block; object-fit: cover;
    }

    .project-body {
      font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-mid); line-height: 1.85;
      max-width: 680px; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }

    .back-nav {
      max-width: 1400px; margin: 2rem auto 0;
      padding: 2rem var(--side) 5rem;
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(200,170,100,0.2);
    }
    .back-nav a {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem;
      font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-mid);
      text-decoration: none; transition: color 0.2s, gap 0.2s;
    }
    .back-nav a:hover { color: var(--text-dark); gap: 0.9rem; }

    @media (max-width: 600px) { :root { --side: 1.2rem; } }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="gradient-bg gradient-asim"></div>

<%- include('include/header-nav') %>

<div class="page-hero">
  <a href="/portfolio/asim-3310" class="back-link">&#8592; Back to ASIM 3310</a>
  <p class="page-eyebrow">Project &mdash; Spring 2026</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">Coloring</h1>
  <p class="page-desc">An interactive generative piece exploring color, form, and user-driven visual composition through TouchDesigner.</p>
  <div class="page-tags">
    <span class="tag">TouchDesigner</span>
    <span class="tag">Generative Art</span>
    <span class="tag">Interactive Media</span>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Main video -->
<div class="video-full">
  <div class="gallery-divider"></div>
  <div class="video-full-wrap">
    <video controls preload="none" poster="/images/asim/coloringSS.png">
      <source src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dijso2iol/video/upload/q_auto/f_auto/v1778204692/coloring_ovfg1z.mp4" type="video/mp4">
    </video>
  </div>
  <p class="video-caption">Coloring, 2026</p>
</div>

<!-- First paragraph block -->
<div class="work-content">
  <p class="project-body">
    Coloring began as an investigation into how digital systems can replicate the intuitive, tactile quality of mark-making. Working in TouchDesigner, I explored how color — its hue, saturation, and movement — could be treated not as a property of form but as a form in itself. The result is a system that feels less like a program and more like a medium, something you move through rather than simply observe.
  </p>
  <p class="project-body">
    The piece draws on the visual language of traditional coloring — the layering of pigment, the rhythm of a hand moving across a surface — and translates it into a generative context. Each pass through the system produces something slightly different, shaped by timing, input, and the inherent unpredictability of the patch itself.
  </p>

  <div class="section-divider"></div>
</div>

<!-- TouchDesigner patch image -->
<div class="img-full">
  <img src="/images/asim/coloringTDpatch.png" alt="TouchDesigner patch for Coloring" loading="lazy">
</div>

<!-- Second paragraph block -->
<div class="work-content">
  <p class="project-body">
    Building the patch for Coloring required thinking carefully about the flow of data — how a signal moves through a network of operators and transforms at each stage into something new. The TouchDesigner patch became its own kind of drawing, a diagram of decisions made in real time, each node a choice about what to keep, what to discard, and what to amplify.
  </p>
  <p class="project-body">
    This process deepened my understanding of TouchDesigner as a compositional tool rather than simply a rendering engine. The patch is not just infrastructure; it is part of the work itself — a record of process made visible.
  </p>

  <div class="section-divider"></div>
</div>

<!-- Code video, no caption -->
<div class="video-full">
  <div class="video-full-wrap">
    <video controls preload="none" poster="/images/asim/coloringcodeSS.png">
      <source src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dijso2iol/video/upload/q_auto/f_auto/v1778204737/coloringcode_c4u4xu.mp4" type="video/mp4">
    </video>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Final paragraph block -->
<div class="work-content">
  <p class="project-body">
    The code behind Coloring reflects the iterative nature of the entire project. Rather than writing toward a fixed outcome, I wrote toward a feeling — adjusting parameters, testing variations, and letting the system surprise me. This approach to coding, more exploratory than prescriptive, felt closer to sketching than engineering, and produced results I could not have planned in advance.
  </p>
  <p class="project-body">
    Looking back, Coloring stands as one of the most process-driven pieces I made in the course. It is less about what you see and more about how it came to be — a record of curiosity, iteration, and the particular pleasure of not quite knowing where something is going until it arrives.
  </p>
</div>

